# ─── Dependencies ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/

# ─── Package manager caches ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# On this machine pnpm keeps its content-addressable store inside the repository
# rather than in a global location, so it must never be committed. It is only a
# cache: `rm -rf .pnpm-store` is always safe, and `pnpm install` rebuilds it.
.pnpm-store/
# pnpm's own debug output, and a stray Yarn install if one ever happens here.
.pnpm-debug.log*
.yarn/
.pnp.*
.yarnrc.yml

# ─── Local environment and credentials ───────────────────────────────────────
# This plugin stores no credentials, but a developer's shell exports may leak
# into the working directory; `.env.example` stays committed as the template.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.key
*.pem
*.p12
credentials.yaml
.credentials.yaml
secrets.yaml

# ─── Build and packaging output ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# `pnpm pack` / `npm pack` output. Build artifacts that ship (`lib/**`) are
# committed on purpose: the browser bundle is hand-written, not generated.
*.tgz
dist/
build/
coverage/
*.lcov
.nyc_output/

# ─── Logs and scratch directories ────────────────────────────────────────────
# `pnpm run smoke` writes screenshots and build logs under the plugin data
# directory, not here; this rule covers ad-hoc scratch trees such as a throwaway
# `.tmp-dsh` profile or a `.tmp-run` workspace.
.tmp-*/
.cache/
*.log
*.tmp
*.temp

# ─── Docs ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Reverse-engineered DSH plugin contracts, the example plugin that mounts
# offline, and the dated verification reports. None of it ships in the package,
# none of it is read at runtime, and none of it is loaded by `pnpm test` or the
# two gates.
docs/

# ─── Agents ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# `AGENTS.md` is the shared context and is committed. A local override file is
# one developer's personal preferences, so it stays out of the repository the
# same way a personal editor config does.
.claude.local.md

# ─── Editors ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# ─── Operating systems ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
._*
.Spotlight-V100/
.Trashes
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
